<div>Dear Ken Kubota,</div><div>IETF has SEAT working group. It works on TL=
S 1.3 extension. SEAT has <a href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft=
-fossati-seat-early-attestation/" target=3D"_blank">https://datatracker.iet=
f.org/doc/draft-fossati-seat-early-attestation/</a>.</div><div>41 high clas=
s CVEs were filed against it: <a href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/d=
raft-intra-handshake-fail/" target=3D"_blank">https://datatracker.ietf.org/=
doc/draft-intra-handshake-fail/</a></div><div>They also provided patch to f=
ix. The patch was never applied.</div><div>Anyone who talks about CVEs is g=
iven "official warning" by chairs.</div><div>Is it in scope of your mailing=
 list <a href=3D"https://listi.jpberlin.de/mailman/listinfo/ietf-discussion=
" target=3D"_blank">https://listi.jpberlin.de/mailman/listinfo/ietf-discuss=
ion</a>?<br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Waqas</div><br><br>
